package tracequery

const ProcessProfileTeaching = "For a process overview use process_profile with pid=<observed source TID> and time_start/time_end. Native TGID identifies members, never a name or marker-PID vote. This returns process_profile.threads with whole-window scheduler states, sleep groups and closed synchronous business hotspots. Read full thread_count, emitted/omitted and unavailable counts before interpreting the top running rows. States.values absent is unmeasured, not zero; percentages divide by the entire wall-clock window. Sleep groups preserve S, non-IO D, proven IO and unknown caller separately; S IO flags are a subset of S. Hotspot inclusive_ms includes nested work and is neither CPU running nor self time; do not add overlapping business names. This membership/state/caller hierarchy is not a call graph or wakeup dependency tree. To explain response impact, follow independently observed wakeup/blocked evidence with wakeup_chain/root_cause_rank; overview rankings cannot elect a root cause."
